-- expect-command: run
-- expect-status: fail
-- expect-stdout: before
-- expect-stdout-not: after
-- expect-stderr: flat_map callback must return List, got Option

-- `flat_map` joins the lists its callback returns. A generic callback whose
-- result is only known at run time and is an `Option` stops the program; the
-- interpreter once read it as an empty list (dropping every `Some`) and
-- compiled code as a list of at most one element.
> pick(x: a) -> a { x }

@ print("before")
@ print(show(flat_map([Some(30), None, Some(140)], pick)))
@ print("after")
